1
00:00:00,383 --> 00:00:01,493
(All characters and organisations in this drama are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,493 --> 00:00:02,593
(Filming with minors followed broadcast guidelines,)

3
00:00:02,593 --> 00:00:03,693
(and generative AI was used in select scenes.)

4
00:00:05,523 --> 00:00:06,523
I have to go.

5
00:00:06,593 --> 00:00:07,863
(Episode 16)

6
00:00:10,493 --> 00:00:11,663
Where's your child?

7
00:00:23,713 --> 00:00:24,783
The one you gave birth to...

8
00:00:30,383 --> 00:00:31,523
Our child...

9
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:34,823
Where is our child then?

10
00:00:54,443 --> 00:00:55,473
To Gyu Min...

11
00:00:56,973 --> 00:00:58,613
You showed her the ultrasound pictures, right?

12
00:01:03,313 --> 00:01:05,583
You told her you would come back after having the baby, right?

13
00:01:09,923 --> 00:01:11,053
Our child...

14
00:01:13,493 --> 00:01:14,493
Where's our child?

15
00:01:28,673 --> 00:01:29,743
On the other side.

16
00:01:40,083 --> 00:01:41,453
The angel must have...

17
00:01:43,223 --> 00:01:44,493
lost their way for a moment.

18
00:01:47,163 --> 00:01:48,563
As soon as they came into the world,

19
00:01:52,663 --> 00:01:53,733
they went right back...

20
00:01:54,773 --> 00:01:55,803
to the other side.

21
00:02:21,023 --> 00:02:22,393
Gyeol must be waiting.

22
00:02:24,033 --> 00:02:25,063
You should go.

23
00:02:36,443 --> 00:02:37,873
Please take good care of Gyeol.

24
00:03:18,983 --> 00:03:21,753
When I have kids later, I will make a baseball team.

25
00:03:23,593 --> 00:03:25,823
Do you even know how many people play baseball?

26
00:03:25,893 --> 00:03:28,593
Of course. It takes nine people.

27
00:03:31,633 --> 00:03:33,663
You want to have nine kids?

28
00:03:33,733 --> 00:03:37,073
- Why? Can we not? - No, absolutely not.

29
00:03:37,133 --> 00:03:40,343
Do you know how hard pregnancy and childbirth are on a woman?

30
00:03:40,403 --> 00:03:41,403
Just one.

31
00:03:41,473 --> 00:03:43,013
Let us just have one and raise them well.

32
00:03:44,443 --> 00:03:45,643
No.

33
00:03:47,413 --> 00:03:48,913
Being an only child is too lonely.

34
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:55,023
Then five. Let us make a basketball team.

35
00:03:56,253 --> 00:03:59,763
Why base our family planning on ball games?

36
00:03:59,823 --> 00:04:02,533
Then let us go with badminton.

37
00:04:02,593 --> 00:04:03,633
Just two.

38
00:04:05,933 --> 00:04:07,333
That will not work.

39
00:04:07,403 --> 00:04:10,203
I have only picked out one name so far.

40
00:04:10,273 --> 00:04:11,273
What is it?

41
00:04:13,243 --> 00:04:15,543
Hope. Kim Hope.

42
00:04:17,713 --> 00:04:18,883
Then for the second one...

43
00:04:20,113 --> 00:04:22,083
I should name them Wish.

44
00:04:22,153 --> 00:04:24,283
Hope and Wish, how does that sound?

45
00:04:24,353 --> 00:04:25,353
That is pretty.

46
00:05:04,993 --> 00:05:07,963
All done, you are dry.

47
00:05:08,023 --> 00:05:09,363
Let us go put on some lotion.

48
00:05:25,413 --> 00:05:28,043
You look so handsome after your bath, Han Gyeol.

49
00:05:29,213 --> 00:05:30,353
Thank you.

50
00:05:37,523 --> 00:05:38,793
People would think he is your son.

51
00:05:40,863 --> 00:05:42,663
Close the door, he is cold.

52
00:05:49,473 --> 00:05:51,573
That mister seems really petty.

53
00:05:52,673 --> 00:05:56,013
I told you. He is as petty as they come.

54
00:05:56,073 --> 00:05:57,313
But he is a good guy at heart.

55
00:05:58,583 --> 00:06:00,213
Hey, you.

56
00:06:00,283 --> 00:06:01,983
We should clip your fingernails and toenails too.

57
00:06:08,423 --> 00:06:09,423
Why?

58
00:06:11,053 --> 00:06:12,193
Why are you staring at me like that?

59
00:06:13,323 --> 00:06:15,763
Because you seem like a really good person.

60
00:06:16,763 --> 00:06:19,263
So I really like you too.

61
00:06:20,863 --> 00:06:22,133
Are you confessing your feelings to me?

62
00:06:26,343 --> 00:06:30,043
How great would it be if you were my dad?

63
00:06:49,233 --> 00:06:52,233
Han Gyu Seo was bragging about hugging you,

64
00:06:52,303 --> 00:06:53,733
so I wanted to hug you too.

65
00:06:59,003 --> 00:07:02,643
It has been a long time since I hugged my Gyu Min.

66
00:07:02,713 --> 00:07:04,243
- Right? - Yes.

67
00:07:07,883 --> 00:07:10,753
But why are you just skin and bones?

68
00:07:10,813 --> 00:07:12,723
You feel even thinner than last time.

69
00:07:14,753 --> 00:07:15,823
It breaks my heart.

70
00:07:16,993 --> 00:07:18,693
You must be going through a lot.

71
00:07:19,823 --> 00:07:22,333
No, my weight is exactly the same.

72
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:26,603
I am not struggling that much, Gyu Min.

73
00:07:26,663 --> 00:07:27,863
You do not need to worry.

74
00:07:28,573 --> 00:07:29,573
Okay.

75
00:07:31,403 --> 00:07:32,743
Oh, right.

76
00:07:32,803 --> 00:07:34,703
I heard Gyeol is staying at Mu Jin's place?

77
00:07:37,673 --> 00:07:39,743
Mu Jin is really Gyeol's rock.

78
00:07:41,643 --> 00:07:44,553
That kid is smart, anyway.

79
00:07:44,613 --> 00:07:46,783
He is smart and even knows how to read the room.

80
00:07:48,023 --> 00:07:51,453
Mu Jin is a really good person, you know.

81
00:07:51,523 --> 00:07:52,723
And incredibly warm.

82
00:08:02,033 --> 00:08:04,433
Tell him to make some room for you, too.

83
00:08:04,503 --> 00:08:05,603
Someone to lean on.

84
00:08:07,903 --> 00:08:09,273
Mu Jin...

85
00:08:09,343 --> 00:08:11,943
is dying to come back to you right now.

86
00:08:12,013 --> 00:08:15,413
Man, he might actually die if you leave him like that.

87
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:18,523
Gyu Min. What should we do?

88
00:08:18,583 --> 00:08:21,053
Are you just going to let Mu Jin pass away?

89
00:08:21,123 --> 00:08:23,553
We have to save a life first, do we not?

90
00:08:23,623 --> 00:08:26,493
You need to give him an opening and show him there is a chance.

91
00:08:26,563 --> 00:08:28,863
So that Mu Jin can come back to you...

92
00:08:30,933 --> 00:08:32,533
Actually, no.

93
00:08:32,603 --> 00:08:34,963
Should I just tell him for you?

94
00:08:35,033 --> 00:08:37,033
That Kim Mu Jin is still my love...

95
00:08:38,233 --> 00:08:40,773
I mean, your love.

96
00:08:42,213 --> 00:08:43,213
Have you...

97
00:08:44,473 --> 00:08:46,113
been meeting with Mu Jin?

98
00:08:48,343 --> 00:08:49,353
Yes.

99
00:08:50,683 --> 00:08:54,023
I see him every day. I am going to see him today, too.

100
00:08:55,323 --> 00:08:59,193
He is the owner of the restaurant where I work part-time. Mu Jin is.

101
00:08:59,263 --> 00:09:00,763
The owner and the Chef.

102
00:09:04,863 --> 00:09:06,763
It is a small world,

103
00:09:06,833 --> 00:09:09,873
and fate is stronger than you think.

104
00:09:09,933 --> 00:09:12,173
I think fate is using me...

105
00:09:12,243 --> 00:09:14,673
to bring you and Mu Jin back together.

106
00:09:14,743 --> 00:09:15,913
Like a bridge.

107
00:09:17,113 --> 00:09:18,583
I might just be...

108
00:09:19,683 --> 00:09:21,013
a crow.

109
00:09:22,413 --> 00:09:25,283
Awesome. Does that make Gyeol a magpie, then?

110
00:09:34,663 --> 00:09:36,363
Why are you eating burnt food?

111
00:09:37,363 --> 00:09:40,703
Spit it out. I said spit it out. Spit.

112
00:09:44,273 --> 00:09:47,943
Are you crazy? Why did you swallow it?

113
00:09:48,003 --> 00:09:50,713
You never listen to a word I say.

114
00:09:50,773 --> 00:09:53,083
Do you not know how bad burnt food is for you?

115
00:09:53,143 --> 00:09:54,983
Are you in a rush to die early?

116
00:09:56,253 --> 00:09:59,453
If I eat sweet food twice, you will beat me to death first.

117
00:10:00,783 --> 00:10:02,053
I mean, how old are you that you still...

118
00:10:02,123 --> 00:10:04,223
cannot make scrambled eggs properly?

119
00:10:04,293 --> 00:10:05,993
How are you ever going to get married?

120
00:10:07,593 --> 00:10:09,693
Where do I even begin to teach you guys?

121
00:10:09,763 --> 00:10:10,763
Move.

122
00:10:13,303 --> 00:10:14,503
What are you doing?

123
00:10:15,573 --> 00:10:17,733
I will make them for you today. The scrambled eggs.

124
00:10:20,043 --> 00:10:21,043
Forget it. I will do it.

125
00:10:21,103 --> 00:10:22,443
You said it is every man for himself.

126
00:10:23,843 --> 00:10:26,683
Are you going to burn them again? Eggs are so expensive, seriously.

127
00:10:27,783 --> 00:10:29,853
I will not burn them. I just have to not burn them.

128
00:10:31,553 --> 00:10:34,653
That is why I am doing it just for today.

129
00:10:34,723 --> 00:10:36,353
I said I will do it.

130
00:10:40,023 --> 00:10:41,693
Hey, what are you two doing?

131
00:10:41,763 --> 00:10:44,463
Are you getting into physical fights now?

132
00:10:44,533 --> 00:10:47,033
- You guys are unbelievable. - It is not like that.

133
00:10:47,103 --> 00:10:49,773
Oh, my heart is just breaking.

134
00:10:49,833 --> 00:10:52,373
What kind of kids act like this?

135
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:55,243
Did I raise you guys that poorly?

136
00:10:55,313 --> 00:10:58,843
How is it that not a single one of you is normal?

137
00:10:58,913 --> 00:11:01,783
- My gosh. - We were not fighting, Father.

138
00:11:03,553 --> 00:11:04,753
Did you check your phone?

139
00:11:05,753 --> 00:11:07,553
Gyu Young got married.

140
00:11:07,623 --> 00:11:09,493
My gosh.

141
00:11:09,553 --> 00:11:11,353
When?

142
00:11:11,423 --> 00:11:12,923
When did she get married?

143
00:11:12,993 --> 00:11:17,833
- No way. - She made a group chat and wrote...

144
00:11:17,893 --> 00:11:19,233
that she was removed from my family register,

145
00:11:19,303 --> 00:11:20,833
and even attached a certificate to prove it.

146
00:11:20,903 --> 00:11:25,343
Oh my, I am dizzy. I must be really in shock.

147
00:11:25,403 --> 00:11:28,613
Wow, is Han Gyu Young completely out of her mind?

148
00:11:29,713 --> 00:11:33,413
I need to lie down. Oh, I am so dizzy.

149
00:11:39,223 --> 00:11:40,923
I got married.

150
00:11:40,983 --> 00:11:42,953
I will start moving my things out today,

151
00:11:43,023 --> 00:11:45,223
and I plan to move into my husband's family home in three days.

152
00:11:45,293 --> 00:11:46,363
Tonight at six o'clock,

153
00:11:46,423 --> 00:11:48,593
I will have a farewell party at Cheonanmun,

154
00:11:48,663 --> 00:11:50,733
so you do not have to come if you are busy or do not want to.

155
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:53,733
(Certified Copy of Resident Registration)

156
00:11:53,803 --> 00:11:57,333
(Han Gyu Young, Daughter-in-law)

157
00:12:00,273 --> 00:12:02,213
You do not knock...

158
00:12:02,273 --> 00:12:03,273
Right, do not do it.

159
00:12:03,343 --> 00:12:06,343
I do not care if you smash the door down and come in anymore.

160
00:12:06,413 --> 00:12:08,183
Was this really the only way?

161
00:12:09,353 --> 00:12:12,953
Even though we lived as one family for over 30 years,

162
00:12:13,023 --> 00:12:14,553
how could you just send a single text?

163
00:12:16,153 --> 00:12:17,853
Do you really have to go this far?

164
00:12:19,363 --> 00:12:22,733
- It was several lines. - Han Gyu Young.

165
00:12:22,793 --> 00:12:25,263
Should we hug and cry our eyes out, then?

166
00:12:25,333 --> 00:12:28,403
You do not even mean that. If I say I am leaving this house,

167
00:12:28,463 --> 00:12:30,633
everyone will set off fireworks and celebrate, right?

168
00:12:30,703 --> 00:12:34,473
What are you talking about? You said you wanted to cut ties.

169
00:12:34,543 --> 00:12:35,873
Without even waiting for me to get married,

170
00:12:35,943 --> 00:12:38,683
were you not the one who said we should cut ties immediately?

171
00:12:38,743 --> 00:12:40,443
Why are you being so clingy?

172
00:12:42,413 --> 00:12:45,683
Do you hate our family that much?

173
00:12:45,753 --> 00:12:47,953
Why ask that now? Do you like them?

174
00:12:48,023 --> 00:12:49,823
Do you love the Hans so much that you could die?

175
00:12:52,223 --> 00:12:53,223
Fine.

176
00:12:54,563 --> 00:12:56,133
Goodbye.

177
00:12:56,193 --> 00:12:58,803
I am sorry, but I will not be able to go to your farewell party.

178
00:13:03,173 --> 00:13:04,833
And...

179
00:13:04,903 --> 00:13:07,873
this is my last request to you,

180
00:13:07,943 --> 00:13:11,313
to your husband and your husband's family,

181
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:13,583
tell them the truth and beg for forgiveness.

182
00:13:13,643 --> 00:13:15,413
If they do not forgive you,

183
00:13:15,483 --> 00:13:18,653
get on your knees and beg until they do.

184
00:13:18,723 --> 00:13:20,883
If they still will not forgive you, then...

185
00:13:22,753 --> 00:13:26,563
- The door is open, so anytime... - Are you cursing me?

186
00:13:26,623 --> 00:13:28,323
Do you think I am you?

187
00:13:28,393 --> 00:13:29,763
Stop worrying about others, Han Gyu Rim,

188
00:13:29,833 --> 00:13:31,493
and take care of yourself.

189
00:13:31,563 --> 00:13:32,933
No matter how much you bring it upon yourself,

190
00:13:33,003 --> 00:13:35,003
raising a child you did not even give birth to,

191
00:13:35,063 --> 00:13:39,173
and blocking your own future. Of everyone I've met, you are...

192
00:13:39,243 --> 00:13:41,273
the most stupid, pathetic, and foolish...

193
00:13:41,343 --> 00:13:43,373
Let us stop here. If we waste any more energy on this,

194
00:13:43,443 --> 00:13:44,913
both you and I will have to go to the hospital.

195
00:13:46,343 --> 00:13:48,113
Before I leave,

196
00:13:48,183 --> 00:13:49,683
as your family register mate of 32 years,

197
00:13:49,753 --> 00:13:51,583
I have one last request.

198
00:13:51,653 --> 00:13:53,883
Find Gyeol's biological parents before he gets any older.

199
00:13:56,093 --> 00:13:58,223
And while you are even one year younger,

200
00:13:58,293 --> 00:14:00,963
make a fresh start while people still call you pretty.

201
00:14:01,023 --> 00:14:02,463
Look at that kid Gyeol.

202
00:14:02,533 --> 00:14:03,533
Since you aren't his birth mom,

203
00:14:03,593 --> 00:14:04,793
he ran away...

204
00:14:04,863 --> 00:14:06,763
and is ignoring all your calls and texts, right?

205
00:14:06,833 --> 00:14:08,733
After everything you did to raise him?

206
00:14:08,803 --> 00:14:10,503
Do you not even feel betrayed?

207
00:14:10,573 --> 00:14:12,943
Why wait three days?

208
00:14:13,003 --> 00:14:16,343
Before I actually break your nose,

209
00:14:16,413 --> 00:14:18,513
just get out of here right now.

210
00:14:26,353 --> 00:14:30,653
I told you time and time again. You can never trust a stray.

211
00:14:30,723 --> 00:14:31,953
Whether it is the twins or Gyeol,

212
00:14:32,023 --> 00:14:33,423
no matter how much care you pour into them,

213
00:14:33,493 --> 00:14:35,163
they will all stab you in the back in the end,

214
00:14:35,223 --> 00:14:36,663
so just you wait and see.

215
00:14:36,733 --> 00:14:38,833
Trust what is trustworthy. Why would you trust people?

216
00:14:42,733 --> 00:14:45,073
One day, a woodcutter was in the mountains...

217
00:14:45,133 --> 00:14:49,843
and met a crying baby tiger with a white cloth tied to its tail.

218
00:14:49,913 --> 00:14:52,483
"After my grandmother passed away,"

219
00:14:52,543 --> 00:14:55,853
"my father was so sad that he passed away a few days later."

220
00:14:55,913 --> 00:14:58,683
The baby tiger said.

221
00:15:00,283 --> 00:15:01,283
(The Grateful Tiger)

222
00:15:02,193 --> 00:15:04,453
That is really sad, right?

223
00:15:04,523 --> 00:15:05,523
Yes.

224
00:15:06,563 --> 00:15:10,533
The tiger really thought he was the grandmother's son, right?

225
00:15:10,593 --> 00:15:13,863
Yes. But in the storybook I read when I was young,

226
00:15:13,933 --> 00:15:17,533
it said that the grandmother also thought of the tiger...

227
00:15:17,603 --> 00:15:19,173
as her real son.

228
00:15:19,243 --> 00:15:23,143
- What? The grandmother? The tiger? - Yes.

229
00:15:23,213 --> 00:15:24,843
The tiger was tricked by the woodcutter...

230
00:15:24,913 --> 00:15:27,143
and thought he was human for a while,

231
00:15:27,213 --> 00:15:29,883
but the grandmother thought, "So what if he looks like a tiger?"

232
00:15:29,953 --> 00:15:32,653
"If I believe he is my son, then he is my son."

233
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:34,323
That is what she thought.

234
00:15:34,383 --> 00:15:35,383
Oh my.

235
00:15:36,723 --> 00:15:39,193
The grandmother knew that the most important thing...

236
00:15:39,263 --> 00:15:42,463
is not appearances, but trust.

237
00:15:42,533 --> 00:15:45,463
- I trust you. - I trust you.

238
00:15:48,033 --> 00:15:49,573
I trust you too, Gyeol.

239
00:15:50,773 --> 00:15:54,643
I know that eventually, you will trust your mom's sincerity.

240
00:15:57,613 --> 00:16:01,213
You are all your mom has in this world.

241
00:16:01,283 --> 00:16:05,253
No one is as precious to her as you are.

242
00:16:05,313 --> 00:16:08,993
I am so jealous. Really jealous. Super jealous.

243
00:16:12,993 --> 00:16:15,193
I cannot really skip work again today,

244
00:16:15,263 --> 00:16:17,933
so I am going to ask Gyu Seo to look after you.

245
00:16:17,993 --> 00:16:19,233
Raise your hand if you have a problem with that.

246
00:16:20,433 --> 00:16:21,463
No complaints?

247
00:16:23,073 --> 00:16:25,403
Wow, you finally answer the phone...

248
00:16:25,473 --> 00:16:26,673
now that I said I would give you the watch.

249
00:16:27,843 --> 00:16:29,943
I am in the hospital lobby right now.

250
00:16:30,013 --> 00:16:31,213
I will come right up.

251
00:16:33,943 --> 00:16:37,113
You piece of trash, you scumbag.

252
00:16:37,113 --> 00:16:38,253
Today, I will make you pay.

253
00:16:55,133 --> 00:16:56,303
Hey, you gained weight.

254
00:16:58,633 --> 00:17:00,673
I am just swollen.

255
00:17:00,743 --> 00:17:03,643
Did you get your teeth done after all that trouble?

256
00:17:05,543 --> 00:17:07,043
They are temporary teeth.

257
00:17:08,783 --> 00:17:11,053
Anyway, I am sorry about what happened.

258
00:17:11,113 --> 00:17:13,123
Violence is never the answer in any situation.

259
00:17:16,723 --> 00:17:19,423
I do not want to talk to you right now,

260
00:17:19,493 --> 00:17:21,323
so just give me the watch and leave.

261
00:17:26,163 --> 00:17:27,763
Here.

262
00:17:27,833 --> 00:17:31,933
The Patek Philippe limited edition you wanted so badly.

263
00:17:32,003 --> 00:17:33,573
I sent it to you on a message as a friendship gift.

264
00:17:33,643 --> 00:17:37,443
There are only three of these in the country, right?

265
00:17:37,513 --> 00:17:39,583
Yes, that's right, you watch fanatic.

266
00:17:41,983 --> 00:17:43,783
Beautiful.

267
00:17:45,453 --> 00:17:48,583
From now on,

268
00:17:48,653 --> 00:17:51,153
if you get caught cheating one more time,

269
00:17:51,223 --> 00:17:53,593
I might make you wear full dentures. Got it?

270
00:17:57,063 --> 00:18:00,133
Are you here to threaten me? Aren't you here to apologize?

271
00:18:00,203 --> 00:18:01,633
Who do you think you are?

272
00:18:01,703 --> 00:18:03,833
Who are you to meddle in someone else's family affairs?

273
00:18:03,903 --> 00:18:05,703
We are not strangers. Gyu Young and I.

274
00:18:07,343 --> 00:18:08,343
What are you talking about?

275
00:18:10,773 --> 00:18:14,983
- Are you cheating behind my back? - Do you think I am you, punk?

276
00:18:15,983 --> 00:18:17,683
Then what do you mean?

277
00:18:20,183 --> 00:18:22,283
When it comes to Gyu Young,

278
00:18:22,353 --> 00:18:25,223
why do I go overboard and act so recklessly?

279
00:18:25,293 --> 00:18:28,363
I thought it was strange too, so I looked into it,

280
00:18:28,423 --> 00:18:30,133
and it turns out Gyu Young is...

281
00:18:30,193 --> 00:18:34,433
my father's great-aunt's...

282
00:18:34,503 --> 00:18:37,433
aunt's uncle's aunt's daughter.

283
00:18:37,503 --> 00:18:39,673
It is the bloodline pulling us together.

284
00:18:40,973 --> 00:18:42,813
What?

285
00:18:42,873 --> 00:18:44,173
What are you talking about?

286
00:18:44,243 --> 00:18:47,443
Anyway, we are not strangers. Gyu Young and I. Right?

287
00:18:47,513 --> 00:18:50,383
What? Why is this guy here?

288
00:18:50,453 --> 00:18:51,483
Oh, you are here?

289
00:18:53,953 --> 00:18:56,123
Why did you let someone into the hospital room so easily?

290
00:18:56,193 --> 00:18:57,653
Do you have no pride?

291
00:18:57,723 --> 00:18:59,363
Oh, I did not just let him in.

292
00:18:59,423 --> 00:19:01,493
He let me in because I said I would give him this watch.

293
00:19:01,563 --> 00:19:03,193
This petty jerk.

294
00:19:03,263 --> 00:19:04,933
Hey.

295
00:19:04,993 --> 00:19:06,833
Are you really relatives with this guy?

296
00:19:07,933 --> 00:19:09,503
Me?

297
00:19:09,573 --> 00:19:13,403
- Are you crazy? What relatives? - We are relatives, Gyu Young.

298
00:19:13,473 --> 00:19:16,313
I am your distant older cousin by blood.

299
00:19:16,373 --> 00:19:18,443
Call me your cousin from now on.

300
00:19:18,513 --> 00:19:21,743
I am sorry, but I do not have a jerk for a cousin.

301
00:19:21,813 --> 00:19:25,283
Our Sung Wook needs absolute rest, so could you leave right now?

302
00:19:26,853 --> 00:19:28,083
Okay, I got it.

303
00:19:28,153 --> 00:19:30,853
I came to apologize, so I will just apologize and leave.

304
00:19:34,723 --> 00:19:35,723
Well...

305
00:19:37,363 --> 00:19:38,393
From now on...

306
00:19:39,903 --> 00:19:43,833
things like this might absolutely happen again,

307
00:19:43,903 --> 00:19:48,603
so live right, you absolute scumbag.

308
00:19:48,673 --> 00:19:50,913
No.

309
00:19:54,013 --> 00:19:55,013
I will get going.

310
00:20:02,183 --> 00:20:03,223
Oh, boy.

311
00:20:04,753 --> 00:20:05,753
Jo Heung Sik!

312
00:20:13,633 --> 00:20:14,633
Follow me.

313
00:20:16,703 --> 00:20:17,703
I do not want to.

314
00:20:18,903 --> 00:20:20,043
That guy, seriously.

315
00:20:23,213 --> 00:20:24,513
If you do not listen to me,

316
00:20:24,573 --> 00:20:28,013
I will torment Han Gyu Rim 115 times more with things you hate.

317
00:20:28,083 --> 00:20:31,213
I will put thumb tacks in her shoes and cockroaches in her pillow.

318
00:20:31,283 --> 00:20:33,023
So follow me, gosh.

319
00:20:35,823 --> 00:20:37,693
What is this? Is she an elementary schooler?

320
00:20:40,593 --> 00:20:42,693
Oh, I am so tired.

321
00:20:52,303 --> 00:20:54,403
Your eyes will tear. Stop glaring at me.

322
00:20:54,473 --> 00:20:56,473
Han Gyu Rim is your weakness, right?

323
00:20:56,543 --> 00:20:58,473
If you like her so much, you should just propose to her.

324
00:20:58,543 --> 00:21:01,713
Gyu Rim and I are just friends. It is friendship.

325
00:21:01,783 --> 00:21:03,653
We are friends.

326
00:21:03,713 --> 00:21:06,453
Whatever. I am not curious about your relationship at all.

327
00:21:06,523 --> 00:21:08,823
Why do you keep interfering in other people's business?

328
00:21:08,883 --> 00:21:10,593
Earlier, you said you were my distant cousin by blood?

329
00:21:10,653 --> 00:21:14,193
- Why would you be my cousin? - We are relatives, Gyu Young.

330
00:21:14,263 --> 00:21:16,993
Are we not descendants of the same grandfather?

331
00:21:17,063 --> 00:21:18,363
Descendants of Dangun.

332
00:21:19,833 --> 00:21:22,333
I left our family register, and now give up my nationality too?

333
00:21:23,273 --> 00:21:26,503
You care about me because I am Han Gyu Rim's younger sister,

334
00:21:26,573 --> 00:21:27,973
but I have already registered my marriage.

335
00:21:28,043 --> 00:21:29,643
I am also out of that family's register.

336
00:21:29,713 --> 00:21:32,883
I cut ties with Han Gyu Rim as of eight o'clock this morning,

337
00:21:32,943 --> 00:21:35,643
and we decided to just be strangers.

338
00:21:35,713 --> 00:21:37,213
- Is that so? - Yes, it is.

339
00:21:41,723 --> 00:21:43,923
It is not like you are enemies who killed each other's parents.

340
00:21:43,993 --> 00:21:46,993
For family members who share the same blood to cut ties,

341
00:21:46,993 --> 00:21:48,323
does that make any sense?

342
00:21:48,393 --> 00:21:50,033
Why do you keep interfering in other people's business?

343
00:21:50,093 --> 00:21:51,963
Do not give me advice either.

344
00:21:52,033 --> 00:21:54,603
I know you spent a fortune paying the settlement money,

345
00:21:54,663 --> 00:21:57,473
so if you have time to be nosy, go make some money.

346
00:21:57,533 --> 00:21:59,573
If I see you in front of me one more time,

347
00:21:59,643 --> 00:22:01,743
I will release snakes in your house.

348
00:22:03,943 --> 00:22:04,943
Oh, boy.

349
00:22:06,643 --> 00:22:09,453
Got it. I'll mind my own business from now on.

350
00:22:09,513 --> 00:22:11,013
It's not like you're my sister anyway.

351
00:22:14,353 --> 00:22:17,423
If you were my sister, I would've broken your legs, you brat.

352
00:22:24,163 --> 00:22:25,233
Mine.

353
00:22:29,303 --> 00:22:30,403
Are you unhappy that I'm here?

354
00:22:33,473 --> 00:22:35,073
Do you hate that your youngest uncle is here?

355
00:22:35,143 --> 00:22:37,373
Don't you miss anyone in the family?

356
00:22:37,443 --> 00:22:40,543
I missed you, Uncle. And Auntie, too.

357
00:22:42,013 --> 00:22:43,413
Thank you so much, Han Gyeol.

358
00:22:46,383 --> 00:22:49,893
Should we eat some apple pie? Mu Jin made it before he left.

359
00:22:49,953 --> 00:22:51,193
Whatever you want.

360
00:22:54,523 --> 00:22:56,063
Is blood type really that important?

361
00:22:57,463 --> 00:22:58,863
What?

362
00:22:58,933 --> 00:23:00,033
Oh, I was just talking to myself.

363
00:23:03,173 --> 00:23:04,633
I don't think it's important at all.

364
00:23:05,933 --> 00:23:09,543
Other than for a transfusion, is it really that important?

365
00:23:09,613 --> 00:23:11,713
Were you talking to me?

366
00:23:11,773 --> 00:23:13,013
No. Just talking to myself.

367
00:23:17,983 --> 00:23:19,423
I miss my mom.

368
00:23:22,383 --> 00:23:23,393
Then go see her.

369
00:23:25,093 --> 00:23:28,163
I miss her, but I don't want to see her.

370
00:23:31,333 --> 00:23:32,663
It's not like there's no way.

371
00:23:34,033 --> 00:23:35,803
You can just see her secretly.

372
00:23:35,863 --> 00:23:37,173
As long as you don't get caught, right?

373
00:24:01,393 --> 00:24:03,763
This spy woman is back again.

374
00:24:03,833 --> 00:24:07,763
I thought I made it clear for you not to come anywhere near here.

375
00:24:07,833 --> 00:24:08,863
Why are you back?

376
00:24:10,103 --> 00:24:12,333
Where are you going? Running off? You spy.

377
00:24:14,473 --> 00:24:16,173
I asked why you're back.

378
00:24:16,243 --> 00:24:20,513
Complain about kimchi being too salty, bland, sweet, or sour,

379
00:24:20,513 --> 00:24:22,683
just to piss me off?

380
00:24:24,483 --> 00:24:28,323
- I have a question. - What is it?

381
00:24:28,383 --> 00:24:31,753
Oh, you want to know where the police station is?

382
00:24:31,823 --> 00:24:35,493
You got orders to plant a bomb and don't know what to do?

383
00:24:35,563 --> 00:24:37,193
Well...

384
00:24:37,263 --> 00:24:40,463
You have an employee named Han Gyu Rim, right?

385
00:24:40,533 --> 00:24:43,673
Could you just tell me where she lives?

386
00:24:43,733 --> 00:24:47,103
Oh, my. I forgot for a second.

387
00:24:47,173 --> 00:24:50,513
Ma'am, you were looking for Han Gyu Rim last time, too, right?

388
00:24:50,573 --> 00:24:54,643
I asked Han Gyu Rim, and she said she doesn't know anyone like you.

389
00:24:54,713 --> 00:24:56,513
She said you're not a relative or anything.

390
00:24:59,553 --> 00:25:01,823
Who are you?

391
00:25:01,883 --> 00:25:06,623
Are you really from the North?

392
00:25:06,693 --> 00:25:09,433
- Oh, my. - Ma'am.

393
00:25:09,493 --> 00:25:12,093
Ma'am.

394
00:25:13,533 --> 00:25:16,133
Ma'am, you don't have to suffer anymore.

395
00:25:16,203 --> 00:25:20,103
You met a noble person, so your life is set now.

396
00:25:20,173 --> 00:25:21,743
Oh, my.

397
00:25:21,803 --> 00:25:25,613
What kind of nonsense is this? And what are these lottery tickets?

398
00:25:25,673 --> 00:25:29,113
I had an amazing dream last night.

399
00:25:29,183 --> 00:25:34,123
Two golden pigs were swimming in the blue ocean,

400
00:25:34,183 --> 00:25:36,723
and then they dove right in.

401
00:25:36,793 --> 00:25:39,793
Then they suddenly turned into dragons...

402
00:25:39,863 --> 00:25:41,523
and ascended to the sky...

403
00:25:41,593 --> 00:25:44,063
Oh, my. The pigs turned into dragons?

404
00:25:44,133 --> 00:25:47,763
Yes. How could I not buy lottery tickets after a dream like that?

405
00:25:47,833 --> 00:25:51,173
So I bought two, just like the two golden pigs.

406
00:25:51,233 --> 00:25:54,473
One for you, and one for me.

407
00:25:54,543 --> 00:25:57,873
I'm giving you luck!

408
00:25:57,943 --> 00:26:03,013
- This is for you, ma'am. - So? So what?

409
00:26:03,083 --> 00:26:07,953
What favour are you going to ask for with these lottery tickets?

410
00:26:08,023 --> 00:26:11,253
I heard you're the landlord of our house.

411
00:26:12,523 --> 00:26:16,093
If you kick out a lucky tenant like me,

412
00:26:16,163 --> 00:26:19,833
did you know your luck will be kicked out, too?

413
00:26:19,903 --> 00:26:22,873
My fortune says I'm a gigolo who brings in luck.

414
00:26:22,933 --> 00:26:24,703
That's enough.

415
00:26:24,773 --> 00:26:28,843
You should've raised your kids better then.

416
00:26:28,903 --> 00:26:31,073
Look at my Heung Sik.

417
00:26:31,143 --> 00:26:34,943
Even though I raised him without a father, he is flawless...

418
00:26:35,013 --> 00:26:37,383
and grew up perfectly fine. Right?

419
00:26:37,453 --> 00:26:42,023
But how can your daughters make it so obvious...

420
00:26:42,083 --> 00:26:45,823
that they grew up without a mother in every single way?

421
00:26:45,893 --> 00:26:47,623
Tell me about it.

422
00:26:47,693 --> 00:26:51,063
They are all grown up and do whatever they want,

423
00:26:51,133 --> 00:26:52,903
they treat their dad like dirt,

424
00:26:54,103 --> 00:26:56,163
and you know I am an outcast in my own home, right?

425
00:26:57,173 --> 00:27:00,173
- Not children, but enemies. - Oh, my goodness.

426
00:27:00,243 --> 00:27:03,443
There is no need to whine like that,

427
00:27:03,513 --> 00:27:06,443
you can give birth to a child, not control their mind, right?

428
00:27:08,783 --> 00:27:12,683
Now, this person here was asking for your address.

429
00:27:15,623 --> 00:27:17,923
This person here, to Han Gyu Rim's father,

430
00:27:17,993 --> 00:27:20,523
you can ask him directly.

431
00:27:21,763 --> 00:27:23,493
As for the house issue,

432
00:27:23,563 --> 00:27:25,993
let us check the lottery results first,

433
00:27:26,063 --> 00:27:27,933
and we can talk about it then.

434
00:27:32,233 --> 00:27:34,403
We are both getting old,

435
00:27:34,473 --> 00:27:36,513
so why does she keep talking down to me?

436
00:27:36,573 --> 00:27:39,043
Is she on a power trip just because she is the landlord or what?

437
00:27:41,413 --> 00:27:44,783
You asked for my address? Who are you?

438
00:27:49,253 --> 00:27:51,923
Who are you, and why are you looking for me?

439
00:27:53,893 --> 00:27:55,163
By any chance...

440
00:27:57,363 --> 00:27:59,263
Mrs. Cha?

441
00:28:01,403 --> 00:28:02,403
Then...

442
00:28:02,463 --> 00:28:03,673
Mrs. Oh.

443
00:28:06,543 --> 00:28:08,803
Have you still not fixed that habit?

444
00:28:12,813 --> 00:28:14,813
Are you going to live like that until you die?

445
00:28:17,683 --> 00:28:20,483
Do you know how long it has been since we last saw each other?

446
00:28:20,553 --> 00:28:22,123
Can you not speak a little more nicely?

447
00:28:23,623 --> 00:28:25,923
I thought you had come back to me,

448
00:28:25,993 --> 00:28:28,123
and my heart was fluttering so much just now.

449
00:28:28,193 --> 00:28:30,333
Rather than going back to you,

450
00:28:30,393 --> 00:28:33,803
I would drown myself in a shallow dish of water.

451
00:28:33,863 --> 00:28:35,963
I tried that too,

452
00:28:36,033 --> 00:28:39,233
but drowning in a shallow dish of water is hard.

453
00:28:39,303 --> 00:28:40,803
It is better to just come back to me.

454
00:28:43,073 --> 00:28:45,743
I will get straight to the point.

455
00:28:45,813 --> 00:28:47,543
From what I heard earlier,

456
00:28:47,613 --> 00:28:50,283
it sounds like your landlord wants you to move out.

457
00:28:53,353 --> 00:28:57,493
It is fine. She might seem tough on the outside,

458
00:28:57,553 --> 00:28:58,993
but she is a softie on the inside.

459
00:29:00,193 --> 00:29:02,023
If I just go see her a few more times...

460
00:29:02,093 --> 00:29:03,893
and beg her to save me, it will be fine.

461
00:29:05,663 --> 00:29:09,363
Do not beg her to save you. I will get a house for you.

462
00:29:10,733 --> 00:29:11,733
What?

463
00:29:12,873 --> 00:29:16,343
- You will get me a house? - In the countryside, not Seoul.

464
00:29:16,413 --> 00:29:18,773
As far away from Seoul as possible.

465
00:29:18,843 --> 00:29:21,383
I will even get you a plot of land so you can farm for a living.

466
00:29:21,443 --> 00:29:24,053
If you want to live as a fisherman, I will buy you a boat.

467
00:29:24,113 --> 00:29:25,553
No.

468
00:29:25,613 --> 00:29:27,883
I am staying in Seoul no matter what.

469
00:29:27,953 --> 00:29:30,523
These days, if you leave Seoul, you can never come back.

470
00:29:30,593 --> 00:29:33,393
When will you ever grow up, seriously.

471
00:29:33,463 --> 00:29:34,893
You do not even have a roof over your head,

472
00:29:34,963 --> 00:29:37,133
so are you in a position to be picky?

473
00:29:37,193 --> 00:29:38,963
If I tell you to leave, just leave. Please.

474
00:29:39,033 --> 00:29:40,403
Take all the kids with you.

475
00:29:44,833 --> 00:29:46,033
Hey,

476
00:29:46,103 --> 00:29:48,673
am I someone who stays when you tell me to stay...

477
00:29:48,743 --> 00:29:51,043
and leaves when you tell me to leave?

478
00:29:51,113 --> 00:29:53,583
Are you here to throw weight around just because you have some money?

479
00:29:56,143 --> 00:29:58,683
You are really hurting my pride right now, seriously.

480
00:30:04,323 --> 00:30:05,623
Please leave.

481
00:30:07,223 --> 00:30:11,833
I am begging you, okay? I am begging you like this.

482
00:30:11,893 --> 00:30:14,803
Please, Han Seok Joong. Okay?

483
00:30:14,863 --> 00:30:16,703
Please leave.

484
00:30:20,803 --> 00:30:22,773
Then tell me a reason why I should leave.

485
00:30:24,743 --> 00:30:26,243
Why?

486
00:30:26,313 --> 00:30:29,713
If I stay in Seoul, is it hard for you?

487
00:30:32,283 --> 00:30:34,823
Are you wavering because you want to come back to me?

488
00:30:37,593 --> 00:30:38,593
Did you not know?

489
00:30:39,863 --> 00:30:41,493
Love always comes back.

490
00:30:44,693 --> 00:30:48,933
It is not about you. It is because of Gyu Rim. Okay?

491
00:30:49,003 --> 00:30:52,773
I am worried Gyu Rim will keep having a hard time if you stay.

492
00:30:52,833 --> 00:30:57,043
I am worried Gyu Rim will keep suffering.

493
00:30:57,113 --> 00:30:59,113
What are you talking about?

494
00:31:02,583 --> 00:31:03,753
There is someone...

495
00:31:05,113 --> 00:31:07,223
Gyu Rim should not meet.

496
00:31:08,423 --> 00:31:10,893
Out of sight, out of mind.

497
00:31:12,523 --> 00:31:15,893
Let us please not hurt Gyu Rim anymore, okay?

498
00:31:16,933 --> 00:31:19,693
Let us please not let Gyu Rim get hurt.

499
00:31:19,763 --> 00:31:22,963
Please. Han Seok Joong.

500
00:31:23,033 --> 00:31:25,203
I am begging you. Okay?

501
00:31:26,433 --> 00:31:29,543
Please, I am begging you. Honey.

502
00:31:34,143 --> 00:31:38,513
With the braised potatoes, steamed perilla seeds,

503
00:31:38,583 --> 00:31:41,383
and the kimchi pancakes and radish kimchi,

504
00:31:41,453 --> 00:31:43,153
the total is 51 dollars.

505
00:31:43,223 --> 00:31:45,323
- Just give me 50 dollars. - My son...

506
00:31:47,623 --> 00:31:49,123
Thank you. Your payment is complete.

507
00:31:49,193 --> 00:31:52,033
We will contact you again before delivery.

508
00:31:52,093 --> 00:31:54,763
- Yes, please take good care of it. - Yes.

509
00:31:54,833 --> 00:31:56,203
Thank you, sir.

510
00:31:57,273 --> 00:32:00,103
Sir. How much is that one?

511
00:32:01,443 --> 00:32:03,743
- Would you like to see the catalogue? - No, no.

512
00:32:03,813 --> 00:32:05,243
Just that one.

513
00:32:05,313 --> 00:32:07,743
Oh, I want to buy it for Gyu Rim.

514
00:32:07,813 --> 00:32:09,643
What is the maximum number of months for an instalment plan?

515
00:32:12,053 --> 00:32:13,453
Let us go, Uncle Gyu Seo.

516
00:32:13,523 --> 00:32:14,553
Already?

517
00:32:14,623 --> 00:32:17,553
- Are you done looking at your mom? - What if we get caught?

518
00:32:17,623 --> 00:32:20,193
I want to go. Because if I keep looking,

519
00:32:20,263 --> 00:32:21,663
I will just want to keep looking.

520
00:32:25,163 --> 00:32:28,803
It is a secret from my mom that I was here.

521
00:32:30,673 --> 00:32:31,673
It is a secret.

522
00:32:49,553 --> 00:32:51,223
- Hello. - Yes, hello.

523
00:32:52,453 --> 00:32:54,763
- Have a good day. - Yes, goodbye.

524
00:33:03,373 --> 00:33:04,503
Han Gyeol.

525
00:33:05,803 --> 00:33:07,943
I miss you so much, really.

526
00:33:17,783 --> 00:33:20,453
(Kim Mu Jin)

527
00:33:41,473 --> 00:33:44,213
I hope you have a peaceful day, even just a little.

528
00:33:59,153 --> 00:34:00,393
Thank you.

529
00:34:07,263 --> 00:34:08,563
Pick one.

530
00:34:08,633 --> 00:34:09,633
Pick what?

531
00:34:11,133 --> 00:34:13,673
Which drink will make you spill everything.

532
00:34:13,743 --> 00:34:16,173
There are so many things happening to you right now,

533
00:34:16,243 --> 00:34:17,873
but I do not know a single thing.

534
00:34:17,943 --> 00:34:19,713
And I am supposed to be your roommate and best friend.

535
00:34:22,813 --> 00:34:25,353
You used to tell me every little thing,

536
00:34:25,413 --> 00:34:28,583
spilling everything to me and discussing your worries with me,

537
00:34:28,653 --> 00:34:31,893
but at some point, you just zipped your lips...

538
00:34:31,953 --> 00:34:34,293
and refused to give me any updates. Do you know that?

539
00:34:36,363 --> 00:34:38,833
You know how much I love meddling in other people's business.

540
00:34:38,893 --> 00:34:41,333
And you. You are not just anyone.

541
00:34:41,403 --> 00:34:42,903
We are friends who swore to become in-laws...

542
00:34:42,963 --> 00:34:44,233
when we have kids later.

543
00:34:48,403 --> 00:34:51,273
If both the head chef and the CEO get drunk,

544
00:34:51,343 --> 00:34:52,573
who is going to run the dinner service?

545
00:34:52,643 --> 00:34:54,583
We have raised the staff to be so independent.

546
00:34:54,643 --> 00:34:57,653
That they do better without us. Don't even worry about it, man.

547
00:34:57,713 --> 00:34:59,513
Okay, fine. What do you want to know?

548
00:35:00,723 --> 00:35:02,183
Everything.

549
00:35:02,253 --> 00:35:03,453
Absolutely everything.

550
00:35:03,523 --> 00:35:05,493
How long Gyeol is staying at our place,

551
00:35:05,553 --> 00:35:07,023
what Seo Hyun is going to do,

552
00:35:07,093 --> 00:35:08,793
what you're going to do about Gyu Rim,

553
00:35:08,863 --> 00:35:11,493
and when Kim Mu Jin will become Jang Mu Jin again.

554
00:35:11,563 --> 00:35:12,733
Man, it's exhausting just saying it.

555
00:35:12,793 --> 00:35:14,503
Should I write it on a chalkboard or something?

556
00:35:14,563 --> 00:35:15,703
You're good at answering test questions.

557
00:35:15,763 --> 00:35:17,033
You problematic human.

558
00:35:19,933 --> 00:35:22,403
Right. Well,

559
00:35:22,473 --> 00:35:23,843
you should know what you need to know.

560
00:35:28,343 --> 00:35:29,343
So...

561
00:35:31,013 --> 00:35:32,153
Gyu Rim is...

562
00:35:36,893 --> 00:35:38,823
Seo Hyun's mother...

563
00:35:45,093 --> 00:35:46,693
So what?

564
00:35:46,763 --> 00:35:49,233
What about Gyu Rim and Seo Hyun's mother?

565
00:35:49,303 --> 00:35:52,573
What, is Gyu Rim actually Seo Hyun's mother's daughter or something?

566
00:35:57,043 --> 00:35:59,213
What? Really?

567
00:36:00,513 --> 00:36:02,313
Did I guess right again?

568
00:36:03,313 --> 00:36:05,653
(Chairman Jang Hoon Tae)

569
00:36:08,583 --> 00:36:10,193
(Hong OK Seon)

570
00:36:13,153 --> 00:36:15,663
- What now? - Let's go get hangover soup.

571
00:36:15,723 --> 00:36:18,433
I sent you a link to the address, so come there right now.

572
00:36:18,493 --> 00:36:20,163
Forget it, I'm not hungry.

573
00:36:20,233 --> 00:36:21,503
If you don't listen, I'm going to tell Seo Hyun...

574
00:36:21,563 --> 00:36:23,633
all about your lies.

575
00:36:23,703 --> 00:36:25,803
Hey, come on. Seriously...

576
00:36:25,873 --> 00:36:27,243
Don't bring your driver,

577
00:36:27,303 --> 00:36:30,213
- and take a taxi. - What? Hey...

578
00:36:31,973 --> 00:36:33,043
Unbelievable.

579
00:36:34,313 --> 00:36:38,453
- Here you go. Enjoy your meal. - Yes, thank you. Hey.

580
00:36:38,513 --> 00:36:40,853
The broth here is no joke, okay?

581
00:36:40,923 --> 00:36:43,523
It'll flush out all the alcohol you drank yesterday,

582
00:36:43,593 --> 00:36:45,293
so drink up. Come on.

583
00:36:45,353 --> 00:36:47,393
It's good if you mix rice in it,

584
00:36:47,463 --> 00:36:50,393
and it's to die for if you wrap it in radish salad.

585
00:36:50,463 --> 00:36:51,463
Eat.

586
00:36:52,663 --> 00:36:54,563
Now, tell me.

587
00:36:54,633 --> 00:36:57,403
What's going on? And what's with the outfit?

588
00:36:57,473 --> 00:37:00,203
Did your company go bankrupt overnight?

589
00:37:01,203 --> 00:37:02,903
Hey, it's fun.

590
00:37:02,973 --> 00:37:05,113
Coming somewhere where no one recognises me...

591
00:37:05,173 --> 00:37:09,383
and enjoying a delicious bowl of spicy knife-cut noodle soup.

592
00:37:09,443 --> 00:37:12,253
Once you get into it, it's hard to stop.

593
00:37:12,313 --> 00:37:13,313
Eat, eat.

594
00:37:15,683 --> 00:37:16,893
Hey, it's getting soggy, eat up.

595
00:37:18,523 --> 00:37:19,523
Unbelievable.

596
00:37:20,823 --> 00:37:22,993
You get weirder as you get older.

597
00:37:28,403 --> 00:37:31,003
- Wow, this is good. - Right? Isn't it?

598
00:37:31,073 --> 00:37:32,733
See?

599
00:37:32,803 --> 00:37:34,443
I should bring Yoon Hee here next time.

600
00:37:34,503 --> 00:37:36,603
She loves noodles.

601
00:37:36,673 --> 00:37:38,043
Oh, boy.

602
00:37:38,113 --> 00:37:41,213
Hey, isn't it actually fun for you two?

603
00:37:41,283 --> 00:37:42,943
Sneaking around behind Seo Hyun's back,

604
00:37:43,013 --> 00:37:45,353
like you're having a secret romance?

605
00:37:46,483 --> 00:37:47,483
Oh, boy.

606
00:37:51,553 --> 00:37:53,093
Hey, by the way,

607
00:37:53,153 --> 00:37:54,823
why did Yoon Hee get divorced?

608
00:37:55,923 --> 00:37:57,433
You were widowed,

609
00:37:57,493 --> 00:37:58,863
but she must have gone through a breakup.

610
00:38:00,433 --> 00:38:01,533
I didn't ask.

611
00:38:02,603 --> 00:38:04,373
You didn't ask her that?

612
00:38:04,433 --> 00:38:05,873
- Oh, my. - Oh, my.

613
00:38:05,933 --> 00:38:09,843
- Hello, you came with someone else. - Yes, yes.

614
00:38:09,903 --> 00:38:13,473
The man you came with recently is waiting in line outside.

615
00:38:16,983 --> 00:38:18,913
When I told him you were here,

616
00:38:18,983 --> 00:38:22,683
he asked me to see if he could share your table.

617
00:38:22,753 --> 00:38:25,693
Oh, I came with a friend today.

618
00:38:25,753 --> 00:38:28,263
- Oh, okay, I understand. - Yes.

619
00:38:29,523 --> 00:38:30,563
- Oh, don't bother. - Who is it?

620
00:38:30,633 --> 00:38:31,633
Eat, eat.

621
00:38:33,363 --> 00:38:34,863
You really are strange.

622
00:38:42,703 --> 00:38:45,513
I am sorry, but since she is with another customer,

623
00:38:45,573 --> 00:38:47,243
she said you cannot share the table.

624
00:38:49,143 --> 00:38:51,713
- Did you tell her it was me? - Oh, of course.

625
00:38:53,083 --> 00:38:54,853
I am currently...

626
00:38:54,923 --> 00:38:56,583
so exhausted I do not even have the strength to stand,

627
00:38:57,693 --> 00:38:59,723
tired, hot,

628
00:38:59,793 --> 00:39:02,793
annoyed, and in pain. Did you tell her all that?

629
00:39:02,863 --> 00:39:04,163
No, well, that is...

630
00:39:05,463 --> 00:39:06,493
What is it?

631
00:39:12,333 --> 00:39:13,973
(Danim-Gil Kalguksu)

632
00:39:14,973 --> 00:39:17,343
Hey, you have to mix it with rice like this.

633
00:39:17,413 --> 00:39:18,973
Oh, hey, there are a lot of noodles right now.

634
00:39:19,043 --> 00:39:22,443
Hey, try eating the rice like this. It is amazing.

635
00:39:22,513 --> 00:39:23,613
Understood.

636
00:39:27,583 --> 00:39:28,823
- This is different. - It is delicious, right?

637
00:39:28,883 --> 00:39:31,593
- Yes, it is delicious. - Eat rice instead of noodles, okay?

638
00:39:33,223 --> 00:39:34,263
Grouper lady?

639
00:39:35,563 --> 00:39:37,663
I feel like I am really going to pass out,

640
00:39:37,733 --> 00:39:40,063
so could you please let me share the table?

641
00:39:40,133 --> 00:39:42,163
I will just sit quietly in this corner...

642
00:39:42,233 --> 00:39:44,233
and quickly eat one bowl of noodle soup and leave,

643
00:39:45,233 --> 00:39:48,073
so if you could excuse me this once, I will never forget this favour.

644
00:39:50,173 --> 00:39:52,313
Oh, yes, please sit down first. Yes, have a seat.

645
00:39:54,083 --> 00:39:55,583
- Thank you. - Yes.

646
00:39:55,643 --> 00:39:56,643
Thank you.

647
00:40:04,293 --> 00:40:06,253
I have not had a single meal all day today...

648
00:40:07,723 --> 00:40:09,593
and had a day like a war zone.

649
00:40:11,933 --> 00:40:14,033
The sun is scorching and the weather is hot.

650
00:40:15,533 --> 00:40:17,403
If I had stood for one more second,

651
00:40:18,733 --> 00:40:20,273
I really would have collapsed.

652
00:40:22,243 --> 00:40:23,943
Oh my.

653
00:40:24,013 --> 00:40:27,443
First, have a glass of this cold water. Yes.

654
00:40:27,513 --> 00:40:28,513
Thank you.

655
00:40:30,853 --> 00:40:33,053
Oh, did something bad happen?

656
00:40:35,623 --> 00:40:37,253
Please do not ask me anything today.

657
00:40:40,363 --> 00:40:42,493
In one bowl of noodle soup,

658
00:40:42,563 --> 00:40:44,563
I will mix all my sadness, anger,

659
00:40:45,963 --> 00:40:47,633
and regrets,

660
00:40:49,263 --> 00:40:50,573
and swallow them all.

661
00:40:52,073 --> 00:40:53,403
- Yes, ma'am? - Yes.

662
00:40:53,473 --> 00:40:56,273
Yes, we would like one more spicy knife-cut noodle soup, please.

663
00:40:56,373 --> 00:40:57,373
Oh, yes.

664
00:40:58,373 --> 00:40:59,573
Extra large.

665
00:40:59,643 --> 00:41:02,613
- Yes, please make it extra large. - Yes, extra large.

666
00:41:14,223 --> 00:41:16,663
Oh my. Are you crying?

667
00:41:20,833 --> 00:41:21,833
Thank you.

668
00:41:23,773 --> 00:41:25,533
Oh my.

669
00:41:25,603 --> 00:41:28,473
Oh, should I order you a cola?

670
00:41:28,543 --> 00:41:30,613
I do not drink cola.

671
00:41:32,373 --> 00:41:34,713
- Could we get a soda here? - Yes.

672
00:41:37,613 --> 00:41:42,283
Oh, what is going on? What on earth happened?

673
00:41:44,353 --> 00:41:45,723
The time I have lived...

674
00:41:48,093 --> 00:41:49,593
I regret it so much.

675
00:41:51,133 --> 00:41:54,733
Oh, you sure regret things often, don't you?

676
00:41:54,803 --> 00:41:57,773
You also miss the days when you ate tuna like kimchi.

677
00:41:59,673 --> 00:42:01,543
Just once...

678
00:42:01,603 --> 00:42:04,773
How great would it be if I could turn back time just once.

679
00:42:06,713 --> 00:42:09,783
Then I would really get my act together and live right.

680
00:42:13,113 --> 00:42:14,453
I would not have let the kids' mom...

681
00:42:15,453 --> 00:42:16,823
leave like that.

682
00:42:18,123 --> 00:42:21,463
- Here is your soda. - Oh, yes, thank you. Yes.

683
00:42:21,523 --> 00:42:22,523
Thank you.

684
00:42:27,663 --> 00:42:29,433
I cannot eat anymore. I think I will get indigestion.

685
00:42:32,473 --> 00:42:34,773
Thank you for sharing the table with me.

686
00:42:34,843 --> 00:42:36,373
I apologize for my behaviour upon our first meeting.

687
00:42:36,443 --> 00:42:39,513
Oh, okay. Oh, no, if your stomach is upset,

688
00:42:39,573 --> 00:42:41,283
just have a glass of this soda before you go.

689
00:42:41,343 --> 00:42:43,243
Oh, just drink it before you go.

690
00:42:43,313 --> 00:42:45,553
I do not drink cola,

691
00:42:45,613 --> 00:42:47,753
I do not drink soda,

692
00:42:47,823 --> 00:42:50,053
I only drink sparkling water.

693
00:42:50,123 --> 00:42:51,123
Oh, I see.

694
00:42:56,023 --> 00:42:57,023
Thank you.

695
00:43:02,403 --> 00:43:04,573
- How much is it? - It is ten dollars.

696
00:43:10,613 --> 00:43:11,673
Thank you.

697
00:43:15,483 --> 00:43:17,613
Wow.

698
00:43:17,683 --> 00:43:18,713
What is his deal?

699
00:43:20,083 --> 00:43:21,083
Hey, by any chance...

700
00:43:22,453 --> 00:43:25,093
Is that the guy who told you that you look ten years younger?

701
00:43:28,363 --> 00:43:29,623
- Oh, my. - Oh, seriously.

702
00:43:31,933 --> 00:43:33,933
Hey, anyway, in many ways,

703
00:43:34,003 --> 00:43:36,263
he does not seem normal, so you should be careful.

704
00:43:37,433 --> 00:43:39,303
He is more normal than you are.

705
00:43:39,373 --> 00:43:42,003
Hey, and what is with the grouper lady?

706
00:43:49,343 --> 00:43:51,183
Hey, Chairman Hong, I am sorry.

707
00:43:51,253 --> 00:43:53,953
- I should get going first. - Why?

708
00:43:54,023 --> 00:43:55,023
It is nothing.

709
00:43:55,083 --> 00:43:57,523
- Oh, could you call a taxi for me? - Hey.

710
00:43:57,593 --> 00:43:59,693
- I have to make a phone call. - Finish this before you go.

711
00:44:00,693 --> 00:44:05,863
(Danim-Gil Kalguksu)

712
00:44:10,103 --> 00:44:11,933
I am going to tell Seo Hyun everything.

713
00:44:13,203 --> 00:44:15,643
- Like my bond with Seo Hyun... - My gosh.

714
00:44:15,703 --> 00:44:19,473
No, because your relationship with Seo Hyun is more important.

715
00:44:21,543 --> 00:44:23,513
You cannot do that, okay?

716
00:44:23,583 --> 00:44:27,723
Seo Hyun no longer loving or respecting you,

717
00:44:27,783 --> 00:44:30,523
- I cannot stand it anymore. - Please answer the phone, honey.

718
00:44:35,663 --> 00:44:37,193
(Husband)

719
00:44:53,943 --> 00:44:54,943
Mom.

720
00:45:01,553 --> 00:45:02,953
Here.

721
00:45:03,023 --> 00:45:04,023
Wow.

722
00:45:12,533 --> 00:45:14,733
Did I ask you to come when you are busy?

723
00:45:14,803 --> 00:45:18,103
Come on, you are the most important thing to me right now.

724
00:45:18,173 --> 00:45:19,703
Should we go out for dinner?

725
00:45:19,773 --> 00:45:22,043
An amazing cold noodle place opened up near my office.

726
00:45:24,843 --> 00:45:28,583
When will my mom feel better?

727
00:45:28,643 --> 00:45:30,243
Should I dance for you?

728
00:45:30,313 --> 00:45:33,713
Mom, they announced the concert dates for Choi Lee Moon Sae.

729
00:45:35,023 --> 00:45:36,023
Seo Hyun.

730
00:45:37,993 --> 00:45:39,153
A person...

731
00:45:40,153 --> 00:45:43,323
as wonderful and good as your dad...

732
00:45:44,533 --> 00:45:46,593
I have never seen anyone like him in my entire life.

733
00:45:49,363 --> 00:45:51,303
Are you being gaslit by Jang Hoon Tae?

734
00:45:53,233 --> 00:45:55,473
Snap out of it, Mom.

735
00:45:55,543 --> 00:45:59,173
Dad is a very bad person. He deceived his wife and his child,

736
00:45:59,243 --> 00:46:01,313
he is shameless, irresponsible, and despicable,

737
00:46:01,383 --> 00:46:06,383
- and he is a massive hypocrite. - Your dad lied because of me.

738
00:46:06,453 --> 00:46:07,853
To protect me,

739
00:46:08,883 --> 00:46:10,753
your dad took all the blame.

740
00:46:12,753 --> 00:46:13,893
What are you talking about?

741
00:46:16,963 --> 00:46:18,733
Mu Jin is...

742
00:46:18,793 --> 00:46:20,363
not your dad's son.

743
00:46:21,803 --> 00:46:23,703
How would that even make sense?

744
00:46:26,033 --> 00:46:27,033
Mom.

745
00:46:28,173 --> 00:46:29,243
Mu Jin is...

746
00:46:30,443 --> 00:46:34,083
the son of your dad's friend, Hong Ok Seon,

747
00:46:34,143 --> 00:46:35,743
nothing more, nothing less.

748
00:46:39,383 --> 00:46:41,823
Why would he tell a lie like that?

749
00:46:43,053 --> 00:46:44,893
Why would Dad protect you?

750
00:46:47,293 --> 00:46:49,123
What did you even do?

751
00:47:04,003 --> 00:47:05,813
The child that Mu Jin said he met...

752
00:47:07,273 --> 00:47:09,083
Honey!

753
00:47:10,443 --> 00:47:12,883
Honey, wait a minute. Yoon Hee, wait a minute.

754
00:47:12,953 --> 00:47:14,153
Han Gyu Rim...

755
00:47:14,223 --> 00:47:17,423
Yoon Hee, we need to talk.

756
00:47:17,493 --> 00:47:20,523
- Seo Hyun, go inside. - What about Han Gyu Rim?

757
00:47:20,593 --> 00:47:22,893
Honey, do not do this.

758
00:47:22,963 --> 00:47:24,763
Han Gyu Rim is my daughter.

759
00:47:26,893 --> 00:47:27,903
What?

760
00:47:30,563 --> 00:47:32,133
The one I left behind...

761
00:47:33,473 --> 00:47:35,103
when I got divorced. Gyu Rim is my daughter.

762
00:47:44,283 --> 00:47:47,383
What is Mom talking about right now?

763
00:47:48,523 --> 00:47:49,553
Is it true, Dad?

764
00:48:06,633 --> 00:48:08,243
Oh, seriously.

765
00:48:11,873 --> 00:48:13,813
Dad, this...

766
00:48:13,873 --> 00:48:15,383
Seo Hyun,

767
00:48:15,443 --> 00:48:17,753
calm down. I will explain everything.

768
00:48:17,813 --> 00:48:20,213
- Seo Hyun. - Get out!

769
00:48:20,283 --> 00:48:23,083
Seo Hyun. Jang Seo Hyun.

770
00:48:23,153 --> 00:48:25,953
Get out of my sight right now, Go Yoon Hee!

771
00:48:41,673 --> 00:48:44,873
Wow. I mean...

772
00:48:44,943 --> 00:48:47,213
I have not had a single drop of alcohol,

773
00:48:47,273 --> 00:48:48,913
so why do I feel completely wasted?

774
00:48:53,913 --> 00:48:56,323
Let me get this straight. So, first of all,

775
00:48:56,383 --> 00:48:59,093
the Chairman is not your biological father,

776
00:48:59,153 --> 00:49:00,253
and Gyu Rim is...

777
00:49:00,323 --> 00:49:02,093
Seo Hyun's Mother's biological daughter...

778
00:49:02,163 --> 00:49:04,563
whom she left behind when she got divorced.

779
00:49:04,633 --> 00:49:06,063
That is why Seo Hyun's Mother...

780
00:49:06,133 --> 00:49:08,503
was so dead set against you and Seo Hyun.

781
00:49:11,373 --> 00:49:14,133
Right. That makes much more sense.

782
00:49:14,203 --> 00:49:16,203
That makes way more sense than...

783
00:49:16,273 --> 00:49:17,613
the Chairman being your biological father.

784
00:49:18,713 --> 00:49:21,113
I will check the kitchen and head straight home.

785
00:49:23,113 --> 00:49:24,783
Hey.

786
00:49:24,853 --> 00:49:25,913
Does that mean you have been...

787
00:49:25,983 --> 00:49:27,883
going back and forth between two sisters this whole time?

788
00:49:29,853 --> 00:49:31,793
They are not blood-related, but they are still sisters.

789
00:49:35,323 --> 00:49:38,433
Then shouldn't we stop keeping Gyeol at our house?

790
00:49:38,493 --> 00:49:39,933
If we keep Han Gyeol at our house,

791
00:49:39,993 --> 00:49:41,433
you two will definitely get tangled up again.

792
00:49:44,203 --> 00:49:46,273
That kid will become the string, the lingering attachment,

793
00:49:46,333 --> 00:49:48,343
and the glue that brings you and Gyu Rim back...

794
00:49:48,403 --> 00:49:50,573
Shut your mouth, you idiot.

795
00:49:50,643 --> 00:49:53,713
Man, seriously. Stop making predictions.

796
00:49:53,773 --> 00:49:54,783
My gosh.

797
00:50:01,723 --> 00:50:02,783
Hey, Gyeol.

798
00:50:02,853 --> 00:50:04,393
Are you with Uncle Gyu Seo right now?

799
00:50:06,723 --> 00:50:10,723
Yes, I'm heading in now, so tell Gyu Seo he can go home.

800
00:50:12,733 --> 00:50:14,063
Okay, see you soon.

801
00:50:24,473 --> 00:50:25,473
Yes, Gyu Seo.

802
00:50:27,943 --> 00:50:29,543
You are?

803
00:50:29,613 --> 00:50:31,413
At Mu Jin's house?

804
00:50:31,483 --> 00:50:34,213
Yes. Mu Jin asked me to watch Gyeol,

805
00:50:34,283 --> 00:50:35,353
so I am on my way back.

806
00:50:36,453 --> 00:50:39,553
Earlier, Gyeol and I went to your store.

807
00:50:39,623 --> 00:50:41,993
Gyeol came all the way to the store?

808
00:50:42,063 --> 00:50:43,663
Yes.

809
00:50:43,723 --> 00:50:46,063
Gyeol said he missed you,

810
00:50:46,133 --> 00:50:47,393
so we hid and watched you secretly.

811
00:50:49,163 --> 00:50:51,603
Why don't you come pick Gyeol up now?

812
00:50:51,673 --> 00:50:53,833
I do not think that guy will avoid you anymore.

813
00:50:54,943 --> 00:50:56,943
And I think we're being too much of a burden on Mu Jin.

814
00:50:58,343 --> 00:51:00,243
Okay, I understand.

815
00:51:00,313 --> 00:51:01,313
I'll head over.

816
00:51:36,713 --> 00:51:37,813
Are you getting off work already?

817
00:51:41,483 --> 00:51:44,183
Did you have to leave work early because of Gyeol?

818
00:51:44,253 --> 00:51:47,653
No, we just didn't have many customers today.

819
00:51:51,693 --> 00:51:52,693
What brings you here?

820
00:51:54,193 --> 00:51:55,403
Is everything okay?

821
00:51:57,603 --> 00:51:58,933
I came to pick up Gyeol.

822
00:52:00,373 --> 00:52:02,103
I owe you so much for everything.

823
00:52:05,243 --> 00:52:06,673
Have you talked to Gyeol?

824
00:52:08,283 --> 00:52:09,283
No.

825
00:52:10,443 --> 00:52:11,983
I'm going to talk to him now.

826
00:52:13,613 --> 00:52:15,183
Okay.

827
00:52:15,253 --> 00:52:17,283
Don't be nervous,

828
00:52:17,353 --> 00:52:18,523
and don't be too scared.

829
00:52:20,823 --> 00:52:23,463
You've raised Gyeol so well.

830
00:52:23,523 --> 00:52:27,263
He's much more mature than Jung Woo, and very understanding for his age.

831
00:52:30,433 --> 00:52:32,833
Go on up and talk to him. I'll be waiting on the first floor.

832
00:52:37,373 --> 00:52:38,673
Thank you, Mu Jin.

833
00:53:09,173 --> 00:53:12,843
I'm sending you the passcode in case Gyeol is asleep.

834
00:53:12,913 --> 00:53:14,513
And the room Gyeol is in...

835
00:53:14,583 --> 00:53:16,683
is the one straight ahead from the living room.

836
00:54:14,903 --> 00:54:16,343
Mister, are you back?

837
00:54:29,183 --> 00:54:30,183
Gyeol.

838
00:54:32,493 --> 00:54:33,493
It's Mom.

839
00:54:37,823 --> 00:54:39,033
Mom...

840
00:54:40,193 --> 00:54:42,933
came because I have something to tell you.

841
00:54:45,073 --> 00:54:46,273
Well.

842
00:54:47,603 --> 00:54:48,673
There was a time...

843
00:54:51,773 --> 00:54:54,143
when Mom was going through a really, really hard time.

844
00:54:57,843 --> 00:55:00,013
It was so dark,

845
00:55:00,083 --> 00:55:03,523
like all the lights in the world had gone out,

846
00:55:05,223 --> 00:55:07,653
and it was so painful...

847
00:55:10,193 --> 00:55:12,633
that I couldn't even take a single step.

848
00:55:22,243 --> 00:55:25,043
But that's when you came to me.

849
00:55:27,643 --> 00:55:28,813
You...

850
00:55:30,683 --> 00:55:32,453
were crying so much,

851
00:55:35,083 --> 00:55:36,953
and since it was my first time being a mom,

852
00:55:41,593 --> 00:55:44,693
I didn't know how to soothe you. I just didn't know.

853
00:55:46,093 --> 00:55:48,003
So I just held you.

854
00:55:49,803 --> 00:55:51,803
And do you know what happened?

855
00:55:53,133 --> 00:55:56,503
You stopped crying,

856
00:55:56,573 --> 00:55:58,273
and in my arms,

857
00:55:59,913 --> 00:56:02,113
you fell fast asleep.

858
00:56:03,913 --> 00:56:06,153
As I watched you sleep,

859
00:56:08,323 --> 00:56:11,423
the lights in my dark world turned back on.

860
00:56:14,053 --> 00:56:15,063
Right.

861
00:56:18,633 --> 00:56:21,163
This baby came to save me.

862
00:56:23,233 --> 00:56:26,303
Do you know how thankful I was...

863
00:56:26,373 --> 00:56:27,803
to have you?

864
00:56:29,043 --> 00:56:30,603
For this baby,

865
00:56:32,713 --> 00:56:34,943
I decided I had to live with all my might.

866
00:56:37,183 --> 00:56:38,753
That's what I did.

867
00:56:40,953 --> 00:56:42,853
I...

868
00:56:42,923 --> 00:56:44,583
lived because of you,

869
00:56:46,453 --> 00:56:47,623
and I still do.

870
00:56:51,493 --> 00:56:52,533
That I couldn't...

871
00:56:54,633 --> 00:56:56,703
give birth to you...

872
00:57:02,103 --> 00:57:03,843
I'm truly sorry, Gyeol.

873
00:57:07,143 --> 00:57:08,513
I'm so, so sorry.

874
00:57:18,223 --> 00:57:19,423
Did I really...

875
00:57:20,893 --> 00:57:23,063
come to save you?

876
00:57:26,793 --> 00:57:28,133
Do you really...

877
00:57:29,563 --> 00:57:30,933
live because of me?

878
00:57:36,273 --> 00:57:39,973
Yes. I thought so.

879
00:57:40,043 --> 00:57:42,243
Thank you for believing me, Gyeol.

880
00:57:46,013 --> 00:57:47,753
From now on,

881
00:57:47,813 --> 00:57:49,883
I will be The Grateful Tiger.

882
00:57:56,423 --> 00:57:58,963
Thank you for raising me, Mom.

883
00:58:26,293 --> 00:58:29,923
- Hey, Gyu Rim. - I will pack Gyeol's bags and go.

884
00:58:29,993 --> 00:58:31,263
Thank you, Mu Jin.

885
00:58:33,063 --> 00:58:34,063
Right.

886
00:58:42,643 --> 00:58:46,413
It has already been one hour past your reservation time,

887
00:58:46,473 --> 00:58:47,913
are they on their way?

888
00:58:49,813 --> 00:58:51,883
No, they are not coming.

889
00:58:53,183 --> 00:58:54,753
Just give me one bowl of black bean noodles.

890
00:58:54,823 --> 00:58:56,323
Excuse me?

891
00:58:56,383 --> 00:58:58,723
You booked a room for eight people,

892
00:58:58,793 --> 00:59:00,593
and you just want one bowl of black bean noodles?

893
00:59:03,223 --> 00:59:06,093
Give me the most expensive dishes from number one to number six,

894
00:59:06,163 --> 00:59:08,203
from here to here.

895
00:59:08,263 --> 00:59:09,663
And give me one bottle of Chinese liquor.

896
00:59:09,733 --> 00:59:12,373
The most expensive one you have. Are we good then?

897
00:59:13,403 --> 00:59:14,943
Yes, understood.

898
00:59:23,383 --> 00:59:25,053
Right.

899
00:59:25,113 --> 00:59:27,353
Father might not come because he is sulking.

900
00:59:27,413 --> 00:59:29,683
The twins might not come either.

901
00:59:29,753 --> 00:59:31,453
Han Gyu Rim already said she was not coming.

902
00:59:33,323 --> 00:59:34,893
But Han Gyu Oh, this jerk.

903
00:59:37,363 --> 00:59:40,533
(Han Gyu Oh)

904
00:59:45,633 --> 00:59:48,273
The recipient has restricted incoming calls.

905
00:59:50,403 --> 00:59:53,943
Han Gyu Oh. Did you just block my number?

906
00:59:54,013 --> 00:59:55,443
I am getting married,

907
00:59:55,513 --> 00:59:57,413
and I just wanted to have one last meal together,

908
00:59:57,483 --> 00:59:59,683
and you dare ignore me?

909
00:59:59,753 --> 01:00:01,823
After everything I have done for you.

910
01:00:01,883 --> 01:00:03,683
When I was in middle school and you were in elementary school,

911
01:00:03,753 --> 01:00:05,793
I got you those honey butter chips that were impossible to find,

912
01:00:05,853 --> 01:00:08,723
and gave you one unopened bag all to yourself.

913
01:00:08,793 --> 01:00:09,993
Darn it...

914
01:00:11,123 --> 01:00:13,463
Where is the bell? Bell.

915
01:00:13,533 --> 01:00:15,063
Please bring the liquor first!

916
01:00:33,183 --> 01:00:34,183
Why are you here?

917
01:00:35,783 --> 01:00:36,783
You told me to come.

918
01:00:37,983 --> 01:00:41,293
- If I tell you to, you will leave? - Yes.

919
01:00:41,353 --> 01:00:42,593
What kind of guy are you?

920
01:00:42,663 --> 01:00:45,763
The kind who comes when you call, leaves when you tell me to,

921
01:00:45,833 --> 01:00:47,463
dates you if you want to date,

922
01:00:47,533 --> 01:00:50,563
and sleeps with you if you want to sleep with me.

923
01:00:50,633 --> 01:00:54,873
Where did you go with Kwon Hee Na? Why did you not answer my calls?

924
01:00:54,943 --> 01:00:57,203
I do not think the condition of you giving me money...

925
01:00:57,273 --> 01:00:59,913
included an obligation to answer every single question.

926
01:00:59,973 --> 01:01:01,543
Does that even make sense to you?

927
01:01:02,883 --> 01:01:05,213
Then why did you call Kwon Hee Na?

928
01:01:05,283 --> 01:01:06,453
Did you not know I would go crazy?

929
01:01:07,553 --> 01:01:08,953
How can you be so shameless?

930
01:01:09,023 --> 01:01:11,083
What makes you so arrogant? You have absolutely nothing.

931
01:01:12,123 --> 01:01:14,093
You are the one who broke the rules.

932
01:01:14,153 --> 01:01:16,023
If you do not like it, tell me now.

933
01:01:16,093 --> 01:01:17,523
I will return all the money I received.

934
01:01:29,343 --> 01:01:31,373
If it's not Kwon Hee Na,

935
01:01:31,443 --> 01:01:32,843
I don't care who it is.

936
01:01:34,983 --> 01:01:35,983
Happy now?

937
01:01:42,853 --> 01:01:45,693
(Gigolo Bastard)

938
01:01:52,633 --> 01:01:54,633
(Kwon Hee Na)

939
01:01:58,103 --> 01:01:59,403
Eight years ago,

940
01:02:00,673 --> 01:02:02,003
why did you abandon me and run away?

941
01:02:05,013 --> 01:02:06,343
I never ran away.

942
01:02:07,473 --> 01:02:08,643
You were the one who ran away.

943
01:02:10,883 --> 01:02:11,883
Is that Hee Na?

944
01:02:14,353 --> 01:02:15,353
Hey.

945
01:02:16,453 --> 01:02:17,953
Kwon Hee Na.

946
01:02:18,023 --> 01:02:20,323
I bought Han Gyu Oh with my money.

947
01:02:20,393 --> 01:02:22,023
If you do not want me seeing Han Gyu Oh,

948
01:02:22,093 --> 01:02:23,423
you should pay me back.

949
01:02:44,413 --> 01:02:46,153
A leopard never changes its spots.

950
01:02:47,153 --> 01:02:49,223
Darn it, Han Gyu Oh, you little bird.

951
01:02:50,453 --> 01:02:53,723
I am going to break your wings and your legs,

952
01:02:53,793 --> 01:02:54,893
so just you wait.

953
01:02:58,793 --> 01:03:00,263
Su Chan.

954
01:03:00,333 --> 01:03:02,133
Why did you call?

955
01:03:02,203 --> 01:03:04,603
I thought you would not answer, so thank you for picking up.

956
01:03:04,663 --> 01:03:06,603
Hang up, man. I am never answering again.

957
01:03:08,943 --> 01:03:11,173
You really want to beat me up, right?

958
01:03:11,243 --> 01:03:14,143
Then do it now. Until your anger is gone,

959
01:03:14,213 --> 01:03:15,683
I will take every hit without saying a word.

960
01:03:31,223 --> 01:03:34,633
What? This isn't the way to our house.

961
01:03:39,473 --> 01:03:40,833
Where are we going?

962
01:03:42,203 --> 01:03:43,203
Gyeol.

963
01:03:45,713 --> 01:03:47,013
What if your mom and I...

964
01:03:48,073 --> 01:03:49,413
go somewhere nobody knows us...

965
01:03:50,443 --> 01:03:51,513
and the three of us live together?

966
01:04:33,893 --> 01:04:35,763
(Love on the Menu)

967
01:04:36,163 --> 01:04:38,493
Is Gyu Rim seeing Mu Jin again?

968
01:04:38,563 --> 01:04:42,003
- Did they decide to date again? - I love it. It is so much fun.

969
01:04:42,063 --> 01:04:45,173
- I am so happy. - Everything will be solved if I go.

970
01:04:45,233 --> 01:04:47,133
Mu Jin and Jung Woo both knew everything,

971
01:04:47,203 --> 01:04:49,003
and made a fool out of me all this time?

972
01:04:49,073 --> 01:04:50,473
If you dare meet Seo Min Ju again,

973
01:04:50,543 --> 01:04:53,113
- we are both dead if you do. - Do you like me?

974
01:04:53,173 --> 01:04:55,643
How could our brother do this?

975
01:04:55,713 --> 01:04:58,283
- If Gyu Rim finds out... - Gyu Rim will die on the spot.

976
01:04:58,343 --> 01:05:00,713
But do not let it shake you.

977
01:05:00,783 --> 01:05:03,323
Just look at me and listen only to me.

